# chktex configuration for the paper template.
# Loaded via `make lint` (chktex -l .chktexrc), in ADDITION to the global
# chktexrc (whose WipeArg entries already strip \cite/\ref/\label arguments).
# chktex ships with a full TeX Live; `make lint` skips if it is absent.
#
# We suppress the heuristic warnings that misfire on math-heavy papers and
# keep the substantive ones (unmatched braces/$, \left/\right balance,
# ellipsis, doubled words). Suppress via the CmdLine block below — this is
# the reliable mechanism (WipeArg's colon syntax is easy to get wrong and
# a malformed entry makes chktex error out).
#
# Suppressed warning numbers:
#   1  Command terminated with space         (false + with "\ ")
#   3  Enclose previous parentheses           (misfires in math)
#   8  Wrong length of dashes                 (we use --- deliberately)
#  11  Spacing around ellipsis                (siunitx/math false +)
#  12  Interword spacing after a capitalized word ("arXiv." etc. — false +)
#  18  Use `` '' not "                        (fires on quotes inside code listings)
#  22  Comment displayed                      (noise)
#  26  Space before punctuation               (fires on ".bbl" filenames etc.)
#  30  Multiple spaces                         (aligned tables)
#  36  Vertical rule / font-command nag
#  46  Non-breaking-space heuristic misfire
# `chktex -h` lists every warning number; tune to taste.

CmdLine
{
    -n1
    -n3
    -n8
    -n11
    -n12
    -n18
    -n22
    -n26
    -n30
    -n36
    -n46
}
